  "id": "COMPOUND:34513 - PROTEIN:1642",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a complex but coherent relationship between the compound in question and Proto-oncogene tyrosine-protein kinase Src. The compound is identified as a target of multiple entities, including ATP-binding cassette sub-family A member 1 and N,N-Dimethylacetamide, which in turn target Src. This indicates that the compound may act as a modulator or inhibitor of Src through indirect pathways. The evidence also links the compound to HCT-8, a cell line that is known to express Src, further supporting a potential role in Src regulation. The integration of these targets suggests that the compound may influence Src activity through interactions with cellular components, possibly by modulating the activity of ATP-binding cassette sub-family A member 1 or other related proteins. The mechanism appears to involve a network of targets that ultimately converge on Src, highlighting a potential role in oncogenic processes.",
